            <ArticleTitle>Solitary plasmocytoma of the distal humerus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1197-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient presented with chronic shoulder pain from a rare plasmocytoma in the distal humerus that resolved following a pathologic fracture. Staged reconstruction of the elbow after resection of the tumor in the distal humerus resulted in resolution of the patient's elbow and shoulder symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
